---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Maitri Shah | Projects"
  description="Benchmark engineering and LLM unlearning project outcomes."
>
  <header class="glass-card">
    <h1 class="hero-title">Projects</h1>
    <p class="hero-body">Engineering projects where reliability, adversarial robustness, and real-world operations mattered.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="mt-8 glass-card">
    <h2 class="section-title">European Cybersecurity & AI Hackathon Championship</h2>
    <p class="copy">
      Designing challenges for a pan-European competition reaching <span class="metric">200+ participants</span>
      across <span class="metric">7 international venues</span>.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-4 font-bold">Infrastructure Contribution</p>
    <ul class="list-clean">
      <li><strong>Onboarding Automation:</strong> Developed post-login HPC scripts that provision HuggingFace datasets and build the full Conda/Python environment to reduce setup downtime.</li>
    </ul>

    <p class="mt-4 font-bold">Task Development</p>
    <div class="mt-4 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
      <article class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-4">
        <p class="tag">Task 1</p>
        <h3 class="project-title mt-1">Image Attribution</h3>
        <p class="copy mt-2">OOD detection across VAR, RAR, Taming, and Stable Diffusion families with <span class="metric">TPR @ 1% FPR</span> as the reliability target.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-4">
        <p class="tag">Task 2</p>
        <h3 class="project-title mt-1">Model Tracer</h3>
        <p class="copy mt-2">Version-level attribution from white-box signals including logits and likelihood traces across close model variants.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-4">
        <p class="tag">Task 3</p>
        <h3 class="project-title mt-1">Watermark Detection (Vision)</h3>
        <p class="copy mt-2">Binary clean vs. watermarked separation with continuous detector scores calibrated for <span class="metric">1% FPR</span>.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-4">
        <p class="tag">Task 4</p>
        <h3 class="project-title mt-1">Watermark Removal (Vision)</h3>
        <p class="copy mt-2">Attack evaluation balancing detectability reduction against image quality constraints using MSE-based utility checks.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-4">
        <p class="tag">Task 5</p>
        <h3 class="project-title mt-1">LLM Watermark Detection</h3>
        <p class="copy mt-2">Statistical detection of biased green-list token distributions across multiple watermarking schemes.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-4">
        <p class="tag">Task 6</p>
        <h3 class="project-title mt-1">LLM Watermark Removal</h3>
        <p class="copy mt-2">Robust scoring over detection evasion, token similarity (Levenshtein), and semantic similarity (cosine alignment).</p>
      </article>
      <article class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-4 md:col-span-2">
        <p class="tag">Task 7</p>
        <h3 class="project-title mt-1">Framework Infrastructure</h3>
        <p class="copy mt-2">Starter-kit and leaderboard automation for reproducible submissions, evaluation consistency, and faster participant onboarding.</p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-4 font-bold">Operational Role</p>
    <p class="copy">Provided <span class="metric">16+ hours</span> of live technical support during 24-hour hackathon windows, resolving coding and environment conflicts in real time.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-8 glass-card">
    <h2 class="section-title">LLM Unlearning (Trustworthy ML Seminar Project)</h2>
    <p class="copy">Evaluated GA+KL, Sequential GA, and SPUL to remove memorized training data from the OLMo-2 model.</p>
    <p class="copy">Implemented a KL divergence-based loss term to balance utility and privacy.</p>
    <p class="copy">
      Achieved <span class="metric">MIA AUROC of 0.529</span> in specific evaluations while documenting the real trade-off:
      preventing utility degradation remains a core limitation of current unlearning methods.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
